    <string name="ut2_intro_one_title">Linux apps on Android</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_one_body">Your Linux environment, terminal and installed apps in one place. Open GUI programs only when you need a desktop window.</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_two_title">Set up Linux once</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_two_body">Choose PRoot, chroot or an existing Droidspaces container. PRoot works without root. The System section shows what is ready and what needs setup.</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_three_title">Find and install packages</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_three_body">Browse Debian and optional Flathub catalogs. Track the installation queue and open installed apps from Applications.</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_four_title">Files, sessions and permissions</string>
    <string name="ut2_intro_four_body">Manage Android and Linux files, inspect running tasks, configure app permissions and launch a terminal. Installing untrusted packages can be risky.</string>
